red institutions, and investment grade corporate bonds. Avidia Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1869 and is headquartered in Hudson, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert D. Cozzone | CEO, President & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 241 people. Revenue per employee of $430K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $100K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Avidia Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $400M market cap on $104M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $24M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 23 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 45.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 15% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 35% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 85/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 44% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Insiders are net buyers (76% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Be Sure To Check Out Avidia Bancorp, Inc. (NYSE:AVBC) Before It Goes Ex-Dividend","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-avbc/avidia-bancorp/news/be-sure-to-check-out-avidia-bancorp-inc-nyseavbc-before-it-g-1","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794574235.742,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.625,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Why Avidia Bancorp, Inc. (AVBC) Might be Well Poised for a Surge","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3020916/why-avidia-bancorp-inc-avbc-might-be-well-poised-for-a-surge?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_8-3020916",